ciaflag.prg: Test for bug 2267, reported and fixed by Mihai:

Problem. ciacore_async_interrupt() moves the idle alarm to rclk + 1 only if
(idleclk > rclk + 1). If the idle alarm is already due but has not run yet, it
later runs with a clock older than ifr_clock, so ciacore_idle() skips
cia_ifr_current() and the new flag raises no interrupt. It is only seen with
the next event: two events, one interrupt.

When. Every asynchronous flag pulls the idle alarm close, so only the first
flag after CIA_MAX_IDLE_CYCLES (5000) quiet cycles can hit an alarm that is due
but has not run (its time fell inside the CPU's last instruction before the
event).

Seen with a 1581 counting ATN edges by FLAG interrupt: now and then the first
edge after a pause raised no interrupt. Only that case was tested; every
ciacore_set_flag() and ciacore_set_sdr() caller shares the path. VIA signals
are not affected.

Fix. Reschedule unless the alarm is already set for the next cycle. With it: 8
runs of 60 s clean, which without it failed within seconds.

;     64tass -o ciaflag.prg ciaflag.s
;     x64sc -debugcart -drive8type 1581 -drive8truedrive -autostartprgmode 1 -autostart ciaflag.prg

Since we can't supply the 1581 drive via the testbench script, it is left
out of that for now.
